  "text": "Two quick ones to finish. Question eight. What is SCD Type zero? A value that never changes once written, like a date of birth, or the channel a customer first came through. Load it once, and ignore whatever later loads say, even when the same row versions its region as Type two. Question nine. What is a mini-dimension? Fast-changing attributes, like age band and income band, moved out of a big customer dimension into a small table of every combination, twenty rows here, with its own key on the fact. The customer dimension stops adding a version every time a band changes, and each order still records the bands that were true when it was placed. Every table here is rebuilt each day, in order: the snapshot first, then the dimensions, then the facts that look them up. Running that order is dbt's job. Next: how dbt builds a project.",
